From d700f0013be2f444ebed2b517a60e0f7cbef56dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivan Verbovoy <145046797+iverbovoy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:11:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] home: on a display with a seam, the free panel beside a
 window is a desktop

With a window on one panel of a display with a seam the other panel stood
empty: only the wallpaper, and no way to start a second app beside the
first. phoc says which panels windows stand on (phosh_private version 8,
panels_taken); with one taken, home unfolds on the other alone as that
panel's desktop - the app grid in three columns, narrowed by its margins,
its wallpaper with it, without the keyboard, which stays with the window,
and without the running cards, which are for the overview.

It moves at the tap: an app started from the grid with nothing open takes
the panel tapped, so home fades out, takes the other panel and fades back
in while the splash shows on the tapped one, and the window finds its
place ready; no fold and unfold to watch, no card of a starting app
pushing the grid down. With both panels taken home folds to its bar
across the display; a panel freed gets its desktop again. Nothing changes
under a fold in flight. A handle along the bottom of the window's panel
pulls the overview up across the display, cards and all, to switch to or
close a window; choosing, leaving or folding puts the desktop back.
---
